.TH SET_ITERATOR_INIT 3 "15 Mar 2023" "CB" "Library Functions"

.SH NAME
set_iterator_init \- Initialize an iterator for a set

.SH SYNOPSIS
.IB #include <lib/set.h>

.IB int
.IB set_iterator_init(set_iterator_t* it, const set_t* set);

.SH DESCRIPTION
The \fBset_iterator_init\fR function initializes an iterator for a set. It takes two arguments: the iterator and the set. The function returns 1 if the iterator is successfully initialized, and 0 if the set is invalid.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.IB it
The iterator to initialize.
.TP
.IB set
The set to initialize the iterator for.

.SH RETURN VALUE
The function returns 1 if the iterator is successfully initialized, and 0 if the set is invalid.

.SH EXAMPLES
The following example demonstrates how to use the \fBset_iterator_init\fR function:

.nf
#include <stdio.h>
#include <lib/set.h>

int main() {
    set_t set;
    set_iterator_t it;
    set_init(&set);

    set_inserts(&set, "apple");
    set_inserts(&set, "banana");
    set_inserts(&set, "cherry");

    if(set_iterator_init(&it, &set)) {
        printf("Iterator initialized successfully\n");
    } else {
        printf("Failed to initialize iterator\n");
    }

    set_free(&set);
    return 0;
}
.nef